{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1787222699,"nonce":"htzmtdB6aMPDjCeK6CALyUjvtU4=","message":"Done — implementing **comment #3's owner ruling**, not the title.\n\n**Recording why the title is not what shipped.** This ticket's title states a rollover gap; comment #3\nruled there is none, because `generation` died with `alert_groups` and a card per re-fire was already\nthe behaviour a rollover rule would have had to preserve. Comments #1 and #2 are superseded, as they\nsay. The ticket was demoted to a cleanup, and the cleanup is what landed. **The title was never\nupdated, so anyone reading it alone would conclude this ticket was a false premise and drop real work.**\n\n**Deleted, root and branch:** `refire_grace_s` and `group_close_delay_s` — nine settings keys to seven.\nBoth were bounds-validated, defaulted from a corpus derivation, patchable and stored, with **zero\nreaders** outside their own CRUD: `refire_grace`'s consumer went with ADR 0040's retirement of T8, and\n`GroupCloseDelay`'s only reader was grouping's `LifecyclePolicy`. Delete rather than retire, per the\nstanding ruling, in the shape of `bd0fb1d`. Migration `00071_no_setting_asks_about_a_re_fire.sql`\nstrips both keys from existing `orgs.settings` and restates the column comment, which had been wrong\nsince `00059`. Gone from domain, DTO, mapper, patch, read-back, repository, OpenAPI, the TS client and\nthe settings UI (`proto-settings-preview.tsx` would have thrown from `rangeOf` for a bound-less key — a\nlive break, not tidy-up).\n\n**Comment #3's \"check before deleting, not after\" was checked, and it mattered.**\n`TestTheReplayWindowIsStrictlyInsideRefireGrace` read `Bounds(KeyRefireGrace).Min` and asserted\n`floor \u003e DedupTTL` and `floor \u003e= 2 × DedupTTL` — it constrained the **grace floor**, never `DedupTTL`.\nThe derivation ran Alertmanager → `DedupTTL` → `MinRefireGraceSeconds`, and only the last link was\ndeleted. `DedupTTL`'s own floor was already asserted independently by\n`TestTheReplayWindowStillCoversHAAndRetries`, which is **re-homed verbatim** to\n`internal/ingestion/domain/bounds_test.go` — a better home anyway, since `identity` no longer imports\n`ingestion` at all. The `DedupTTL` comment now derives its number from the transport alone. **No live\nbound lost its stated derivation, and no assertion was weakened** — the other tests deleted here read\nconstants that no longer exist, each tombstoned where it stood.\n\n**Both halves of the unenforced \"pin\" are gone**, so the `4aea61e` trap is not left half-deleted: both\n`1200 * time.Second` literals, `TestGroupCloseDelayDoesNotDefeatTheRefireGrace` (which only ever\ncompared the two *defaults* — operators could always contradict them), and the UI's cross-knob read.\n\nAlso cleared: five prose sites in `platform/config`, nine live `refire_grace_s` fixtures in\n`config/tuning_test.go` re-based on `resolve_grace_s` with every assertion preserved, the\n`.env.example` and Helm `values.yaml` examples, ~189 lines of dead guidance in `docs/setup/tuning.md`,\nand a **supersession banner on ADR 0040**, which still asserted the setting \"stays — under its own\nname, in `orgs.settings`, with its bounds unchanged\". That contradiction was found in audit and is\nexactly the ghost reference the delete-don't-retire ruling exists to prevent.\n\n**Retitle still owed** (comment #3's own suggestion): *\"`refire_grace_s` and `group_close_delay_s` are\norg-facing settings that decide nothing, and they leave with `alert_groups`\"*. Closing on the ruling,\nnot the title.","files":null}]}